# uForth Native C/C++ Extension System

Architecture and stable core native functions reference for `natives/`.

> [!NOTE]
> This documentation describes the overall architecture and main core native module (`natives/core.cpp`). For reference on other available native modules (e.g. `sys.cpp`, `display.cpp`, `block.cpp`, `reactor.cpp`, `lora.cpp`, `gps.cpp`, `ble.cpp`, `i2c.cpp`, `ir.cpp`), refer directly to the respective `.cpp` files in `natives/`. It is not required to update this document when adding or extending native modules.

---

## 1. Architecture & Dispatch Mechanism

uForth connects Forth code to C/C++ functions via opcode `CALLC` (44):

1. **Registration**: `forth_register("name", fn)` assigns a 1-based ID (up to `MAX_NATIVES` = 128), stores `fn` in `_fns[id]`, and calls `forth_define_native("name", id)` which compiles:
   ```forth
   : name LIT id CALLC EXIT ;
   ```
2. **Dispatch**: When the VM hits `CALLC`, `c_handle()` pops `id` and executes `forth_dispatch(id)` -> `_fns[id]()`.
3. **Two-Phase & Dynamic Module Registration**:
   - Native modules are declared in `natives_internal.h` via `struct NativeModule` (`name`, `check_word`, `bindings`, `definitions`, `bootstrap`).
   - **Bootstrap Modules** (`bootstrap = true`, e.g. `core`, `block`): Registered automatically at boot. `forth_natives_register_bindings()` runs primitive C++ bindings before `uforth_load_core()`, and `forth_natives_register_definitions()` loads high-level Forth definitions after `uforth_load_core()`.
   - **On-Demand Modules** (`bootstrap = false`, e.g. `sys`, `display`, `reactor`, `lora`, `gps`): Loaded dynamically at runtime using the Forth word `use <module>` (e.g. `use sys`, `use display`).
   - **Module Dependencies**: Certain modules automatically load required dependencies (e.g. `use lora` and `use gps` automatically load `reactor` first).

---

## 2. Core Native Functions Reference

Stable console I/O, commenting, timing, and dictionary inspection native functions (`natives/core.cpp`).

| Forth Word | C++ Handler | Stack Effect | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `emit` | `fn_emit` | `( char -- )` | Output single ASCII character via `forth_output()` |
| `cr` | `fn_cr` | `( -- )` | Output a newline (`\n`) |
| `.` | `fn_dot` | `( n -- )` | Output 64-bit `DCELL` integer followed by a space |
| `words` | `fn_words` | `( -- )` | Walk dictionary linked list and print all word names |
| `\` | `fn_line_comment` | `( -- )` *(IMM)* | Line comment: skip TIB input to end of line |
| `(` | `fn_paren_comment` | `( -- )` *(IMM)* | Block comment: skip TIB input until closing `)` |
| `key` | `fn_key` | `( -- ascii )` | Blocking key press read (del=8, enter=13, exit=27) |
| `key?` | `fn_key_query` | `( -- ascii \| 0 )` | Non-blocking key press check (returns ASCII code or 0) |
| `ms` | `fn_ms` | `( ms -- )` | Non-blocking RTOS delay in milliseconds (`vTaskDelay`) |
| `us` | `fn_us` | `( us -- )` | Microsecond delay (`delayMicroseconds`) |
| `s"` | `fn_s_quote` | `( "text" -- cstr )` *(IMM)* | Parse literal string to RAM, push `cstr` |
| `s.` | `fn_s_dot` | `( cstr -- )` | Print null-terminated C-string to `forth_output()` |
| `type` | `fn_type` | `( addr len -- )` | Print `len` characters from `addr` via `forth_output()` |
| `slen` | `fn_slen` | `( cstr -- len )` | Compute C-string length using libc `strlen()` |
| `scount` | `fn_scount` | `( cstr -- addr len )` | Push C-string address and length pair |
| `s=` | `fn_seq` | `( s1 s2 -- flag )` | Compare two C-strings using libc `strcmp()` |
| `dict>s` | `fn_dict_to_s` | `( dict_addr ram_addr -- len )` | Unpack dict packed string into RAM C-string (`\0`) |
| `s>dict` | `fn_s_to_dict` | `( ram_addr -- dict_addr )` | Pack RAM C-string into dictionary |
| `*/` | `fn_star_slash` | `( n1 n2 n3 -- [n1*n2]/n3 )` | Rational scaling with 128-bit overflow fallback |
| `*/mod` | `fn_star_slash_mod` | `( n1 n2 n3 -- rem quot )` | Rational scaling with remainder |
| `u*` | `fn_u_mul` | `( u1 u2 -- u3 )` | Micro fixed-point multiplication: `(u1*u2)/1000000` |
| `u/` | `fn_u_div` | `( u1 u2 -- u3 )` | Micro fixed-point division: `(u1*1000000)/u2` |
| `u.` | `fn_u_dot` | `( u -- )` | Print micro fixed-point formatted decimal |

### On-Demand Math Modules (`use math` / `use float`)

#### Module `math` (`use math`) - Micro Fixed-Point Math:
| Forth Word | Stack Effect | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `usqrt` | `( u -- res )` | Exact integer square root in micro units |
| `usin` | `( angle -- sin )` | CORDIC integer sine in micro-radians |
| `ucos` | `( angle -- cos )` | CORDIC integer cosine in micro-radians |
| `utan` | `( angle -- tan )` | CORDIC integer tangent |
| `uatan2` | `( y x -- angle )` | CORDIC four-quadrant arctangent |
| `uln` | `( u -- res )` | Natural logarithm in micro units |
| `uexp` | `( u -- res )` | Exponential ($e^u$) in micro units |
| `upow` | `( base exp -- res )` | Power ($base^{exp}$) in micro units |

#### Module `float` (`use float`) - Hardware 32-bit FPU:
| Forth Word | Stack Effect | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `f+`, `f-`, `f*`, `f/` | `( f1 f2 -- f3 )` | Hardware FPU arithmetic |
| `f.` | `( f -- )` | Output 32-bit float to console |
| `fsqrt`, `fsin`, `fcos`, `ftan` | `( f -- res )` | Hardware / libc single-precision math |
| `fatan2` | `( y x -- angle )` | Hardware / libc single-precision atan2 |
| `fexp`, `fln`, `fpow` | `( ... -- res )` | Single-precision transcendental functions |
| `u>f`, `f>u` | `( u -- f )` / `( f -- u )` | Bridge conversions between micro and float |
| `s>f`, `f>s` | `( n -- f )` / `( f -- n )` | Bridge conversions between integer and float |

### High-Level Core Definitions (`core_definitions`)
| Forth Word | Forth Definition | Stack Effect | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `count` | `: count dup 1+ swap 0 +c@ ;` | `( cstr -- addr len )` | Convert counted string (`cstr`) to standard Forth `( addr len )` pair |

---

## 3. Creating & Extending Native Modules

To create a new native module in `natives/`:

1. **No Separate `.h` Files**: Do **NOT** create individual per-module `.h` header files (e.g., `lora.h`, `gps.h`, `reactor.h`). Single-purpose header files create redundant `#pragma once` boilerplate and header pollution.
2. **Centralized Internal Contract (`natives_internal.h`)**: Declare module binding and definition prototypes directly inside `natives/natives_internal.h`:
   ```cpp
   void xxx_bindings(void);
   void xxx_definitions(void); // optional
   ```
3. **Single Include**: Each module `.cpp` file in `natives/` includes only:
   ```cpp
   #include "natives_internal.h"
   ```
4. **Implement Handlers**: Implement native C++ primitive handlers reading/writing stack via `dpop()` / `dpush()`.
5. **Two-Phase Registration**:
   - Inside `xxx_bindings()`, register primitive handlers via `forth_register("forth-name", fn)`.
   - Inside `xxx_definitions()`, define high-level Forth words or register reactor services via `uforth_interpret()`.
6. **Module Table Entry**: Register the module in the `get_native_modules()` array inside `natives/natives_internal.h`, specifying its name, check word, binding/definition functions, and `bootstrap` flag.
7. **String Buffer Standard**: All data buffers written by native modules (e.g. `lora-read`, `gps-pos-str`) must write clean null-terminated C-strings starting directly at `buf[0]` (with `buf[len] = '\0'`). Do not prepend length-prefix bytes.
